---
// THE ECOSYSTEM, AS A STANDING STRUCTURE — Community ∞ Care standing on
// Platform standing on Business (founder 2026-08-08: "business is the bottom,
// which supports the platform, which supports community and care side by side
// with an infinity between the two").
//
// A COMPONENT, NOT A COPY (founder 2026-08-08: "the boxes with the links, etc,
// why are they missing for the platform?"). This block used to live inline in
// the About page, and the weave decks retyped its words as a plain list — so
// the cards, the C/Si marks and the "Learn more" links vanished on the decks.
// Both surfaces render THIS now. Change it once, it changes everywhere.
//
// The 2x2 grid it replaced said "four equal things", and drew something false
// besides: a half-width Business sat under Community, which reads as Business
// supporting Community alone. A foundation has to be at least as wide as what
// it carries, so the two silicon strata run full width and the two carbon
// panels stand on them. Read bottom-up it's the thesis in one picture —
// silicon holds up what carbon does with it.
//
// `alpha` (founder 2026-08-08, the show-where-you're-at lens): stamps a big
// ALPHA label on Community and Care. The weave decks turn it on — partners
// should see the maturity honestly; About leaves it off unless the founder
// says otherwise.
export interface Props { alpha?: boolean }
const { alpha = false } = Astro.props;
---
<div class="weco">
  <div class="weco__pair">
    <div class="wcol">
      {alpha && <span class="walpha">Alpha</span>}
      <span class="wcol-el wcol-el--c" aria-hidden="true">C</span>
      <h3 class="wcol-title">Community</h3>
      <p>The corrective social network, where you can connect, host events, organize in groups, curate community and manage your schedule — one trusted web for your whole life, with no follower counts, no leaderboards, and nothing to perform for.</p>
      <a href="/signup" class="wlink">Join the network →</a>
    </div>
    <span class="weco__inf" aria-hidden="true">∞</span>
    <div class="wcol">
      {alpha && <span class="walpha">Alpha</span>}
      <span class="wcol-el wcol-el--c" aria-hidden="true">C</span>
      <h3 class="wcol-title">Care</h3>
      <p>The Concierge service — a holistic, quantum healthcare system where your care team forms around you, while human wisdom and AI work together to track your Web of Wellbeing and coordinate the next, best step in your journey of healing and realizing your full potential.</p>
      <a href="/care" class="wlink">Learn more about the care model →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="weco__joint">each one feeds the other — and both rest on</p>
  <div class="wcol wcol--base">
    {alpha && <span class="walpha walpha--si">Alpha</span>}
    <span class="wcol-el wcol-el--si" aria-hidden="true">Si</span>
    <div class="weco__basehead">
      <h3 class="wcol-title">Platform</h3>
      <a href="/platform" class="wlink">Learn more about the platform →</a>
    </div>
    <p>How the technology fuels the new economy and culture — one ecosystem where people, plants, animals, elements and land collaborate to restore individual, social and ecological harmony.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wcol wcol--base">
    {alpha && <span class="walpha walpha--si">Alpha</span>}
    <span class="wcol-el wcol-el--si" aria-hidden="true">Si</span>
    <div class="weco__basehead">
      <h3 class="wcol-title">Economy</h3>
      <a href="/economy" class="wlink">Learn more about the economy →</a>
    </div>
    <p>Current-cy — a transparent, dollar-pegged ledger that maps what was actually contributed against what the market pays for it. Not just time, but the wisdom, skill and risk behind it, counted for people, plants, animals and land alike, and translatable back into the economy we are all still beholden to.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wcol wcol--base wcol--carbon">
    {alpha && <span class="walpha">In Development</span>}
    <span class="wcol-el wcol-el--c" aria-hidden="true">C</span>
    <div class="weco__basehead">
      <h3 class="wcol-title">Business</h3>
      <a href="/business" class="wlink">Learn more about the business model →</a>
    </div>
    <p>How the model supports the mission — a lean nonprofit with no investors to pay, radically collaborating with pilot partners to create an ecosystem where revenue flows back into expanding access to goods, resources and care for those in the network.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .weco { margin-top: var(--s-6); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s-3); }
  .weco__pair {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr;
    align-items: center; gap: var(--s-3);
  }
  /* Community and Care don't sit in sequence, they feed each other — the
     lemniscate is the claim, drawn on the seam between them. */
  .weco__inf {
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 34px; line-height: 1;
    color: var(--peach); user-select: none;
  }
  .weco__joint {
    margin: var(--s-2) 0 var(--s-1); text-align: center;
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-faint);
  }
  .wcol {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s-3);
    padding: var(--s-6); background: var(--bone-warm);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg); border: 2px solid var(--peach);
    position: relative;
  }
  /* Business is CARBON (founder 2026-08-08): the model is human decisions
     about how money moves, so it wears C and peach even though it sits at the
     bottom of the stack. Platform and Economy above it are the silicon layers
     — the machinery those decisions run on. Declared after .wcol--base so its
     border colour wins. */
  /* The strata read as ground, not as bigger cards: wide, low, and laid out
     sideways so the eye passes along them rather than dwelling. */
  .wcol--base {
    /* Wide enough that "Learn more about the business model" holds one line —
       at 200px it wrapped and made Business taller than Platform. */
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 280px 1fr;
    align-items: start; gap: var(--s-5);
    padding: var(--s-5) var(--s-6);
    border-color: var(--sky);
  }
  /* The link rides under the title, in the column that was otherwise empty
     (founder 2026-08-08) — it fills the gap and takes a line off the height,
     which is the standing rule: compact, nothing hollow, more above the fold. */
  .weco__basehead { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s-2); align-items: flex-start; }
  .wcol--carbon { border-color: var(--peach); }
  /* Each block wears its element in the corner — C on the carbon side,
     Si on the silicon side, echoing the tiles on the About page. */
  .wcol-el {
    position: absolute; top: 12px; right: 16px;
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--t-lg); line-height: 1;
  }
  .wcol-el--c { color: var(--peach-deep); }
  .wcol-el--si { color: var(--sky); }
  /* The maturity stamp (founder 2026-08-08): big, honest, half-out of the
     card's top edge — the app's EXAMPLE-bubble idiom, grown up. Straight, no
     tilt (founder), and coloured by the card's element. */
  .walpha {
    position: absolute; top: -13px; left: 18px;
    padding: 3px 14px; border-radius: var(--r-full);
    background: var(--bone); border: 1.5px dashed var(--peach);
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--peach-deep);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  /* Stamps follow their card's element: peach for carbon, sky for silicon. */
  .walpha--si { border-color: var(--sky); color: var(--sky); }
  .wcol-title { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--t-xl); color: var(--ink); font-weight: 400; }
  .wcol p { font-size: var(--t-md); line-height: var(--lh-normal); color: var(--ink-muted); }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .weco__pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .weco__inf { text-align: center; }
    .wcol--base { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--s-3); }
  }
</style>
